d reaction.\nArguments:\n- molecule_smiles (str, required): SMILES string of the target molecule.\n- functional_groups_broken (list[str] | None, optional, default: None): List of functional groups that are broken when the template is applied in the forward reaction. None will result in not filtering with this criterion.\n- functional_groups_formed (list[str] | None, optional, default: None): List of functional groups that are formed when the template is applied in the forward reaction. None will result in not filtering with this criterion.\n- bonds_formed (list[str] | None, optional, default: None): List of bonds that are formed in the forward reaction (e.g., \"6-6\", \"6-8\"). None will result in not filtering with this criterion.\n- bonds_broken (list[str] | None, optional, default: None): List of bonds that are broken in the forward reaction (e.g., \"6-6\", \"6-8\"). None will result in not filtering with this criterion.\n- bonds_order_changed (list[str] | None, optional, default: None): List of bonds whose order is changed in the forward reaction (e.g., \"6-6 (1.0->2.0)\"). None will result in not filtering with this criterion.\n- limit (int, optional, default: 10): Maximum number of templates to return. Default is 10.\n\nTool: get_template\nDescription: Retrieves a retrosynthetic template and other information by its ID.\nArguments:\n- template_id (str, required): Identifier of the retrosynthetic template to retrieve.\n\nTool: get_available_functional_groups\nDescription: Returns a list of available functional groups for querying the database.\nArguments:\n\n\nTool: deprotect_molecule\nDescription: Removes protecting groups from a molecule represented by a SMILES string.\nArguments:\n- molecule_smiles (str, required): SMILES string of the molecule with protecting groups.\n\nTool: detect_functional_groups\nDescription: Detects functional groups in a molecule represented by a SMILES string.\nArguments:\n- smiles (str, required): SMILES string of the molecule to a